<title>UK: BA up after UK sets conditions on alliance.</title>
<headline>BA up after UK sets conditions on alliance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Airways rose in early trade on Monday after Friday's late UK government statement that it would clear the planned alliance with American Airlines if the two gave up 168 Heathrow landing slots.</p>
<p>BA shares were up 4-1/2p at 584 by 0816 GMT.</p>
<p>A report in the Sunday Telegraph said BA wanted 800 million stg for the landing rights, though the Sunday Times said BA would reap only 180 million stg from the sale.</p>
<p>BA said only that it wanted a fair market value for the slots. The UK conditions were less tough than some observers had expected.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
